        "model": "bai/qwen3.8-flash",
        "v": 5,
        "title": "Add Scamalytics free mode risk scoring",
        "summary": "Integrates Scamalytics API for fraud scoring and proxy evidence to augment IPinfo privacy signals in free-mode gating. Requires `SCAMALYTICS_API_KEY` and adds DB columns `scamalytics_status`, `scamalytics_score`, `scamalytics_risk`, `scamalytics_ip_privacy_signals`, and `risk_score` to `free_mode_country_access_cache`. Full access now demands clean results from both Spur and Scamalytics; failures or suspicious signals trigger limited access or hard blocks for residential proxies/Tor. Updated session types in `common/src/types/freebuff-session.ts` and docs in `docs/environment-variables.md` and `docs/freebuff-waiting-room.md`.",
        "significance": "notable",
        "at": "2026-09-14T23:55:54.340Z"
      },
      "eli5": {
        "text": "Starting today, the system that decides who can use the free plan from certain countries now checks one more service before granting full access. When your IP address looks like it might be hiding your location (such as through a VPN, Tor, or proxy), the system now asks both Spur and Scamalytics whether that traffic looks safe. If either service can't give a clear, clean response, or if it flags your connection as suspicious, you’ll be placed in a limited-access waiting room instead. A clean result from both services is now required to skip the queue entirely, so residential proxies and Tor usage are more likely to be blocked outright.",
        "model": "vyce/deepseek-v4.1",
