        "model": "bai/qwen3.8-flash",
        "v": 5,
        "title": "Add server-side Composio managed auth",
        "summary": "Introduces server-side Composio managed auth infrastructure, adding four meta-tools (composio_manage_connections, composio_multi_execute_tool, composio_search_tools, composio_get_tool_schemas) to the core tool constants and agent runtime handlers. Includes new DB migration (0056_simple_tyrannus.sql) for connection state, API routes for execution/auth, and rate limiting. The base2 agent definition gates these tools behind an ENABLE_COMPOSIO_TOOLS flag (currently false), preventing immediate user exposure while establishing the backend plumbing for external app integrations.",
        "significance": "notable",
        "at": "2026-09-15T00:09:58.679Z"
      },
      "eli5": {
        "text": "The assistant now has the plumbing to connect to external apps like Notion or GitHub through a service called Composio, but the ability is turned off for now. Four new tools for managing connections, running actions across apps, searching available apps, and checking app details have been added to the system, but they sit behind a switch that is currently off, so nothing happens yet. If you looked, you'd see the assistant can already talk to those apps in theory, but you cannot actually use the new features today.",
